{"id":"9e940c5e-51c4-4630-99b3-9f7232c7147a","kind":"note","ref":{"span":"a4eb2d27eddc588a","key":"bablr1","file":"packages/editor/workbench/capability-confirm.ts","baseline":{"blob":"c24ee3be3291fc5d9a5f6b583da0792bc231fbe8","start":0,"end":46},"shape":{"type":"ImportDeclaration","atoms":["import","type","{","Hub","}","from","\"","@brianjenkins94/hub","\""]},"context":{"after":"2c1cb6475bc215a0"}},"payload":{"text":"Capabilities that shrink as well as grow: an allow rule in the policy is confirmed by the runs that use it. One that no test run\nkept here has used, over enough of them to say, is a problem on the rule, in Problems, with a quick fix that takes it out\n(packages/silo/README.md: \"The join allows what no run used\"). It's a person's to remove: code may need it where no test goes,\nan error's path, say. Runs only say what ran, so a rule about anything but a call's capability and resource isn't judged.\n\nWhat a run used comes from its record (test-runs.ts), read again as each ends. And whether the code could still make the\ncall at all: what each of the workspace's code files can do (lib's `detect`, a scan of its text — a capability, never what\nit reaches), read once a rule goes unused. None that can, and the rule is likely left over (a dependency's call may still\nneed it: what a package can do is the baseline's); a file that can, and it's a test that reaches it that's missing.","wrote":["Brian Jenkins"]},"author":"local","createdAt":"2026-11-22T17:11:52.422Z","updatedAt":"2026-11-22T17:11:52.422Z"}
{"id":"bd3c5c44-698b-401c-867f-0f01090a928c","kind":"note","ref":{"span":"7395a0b97eddb25e","key":"bablr1","file":"packages/editor/workbench/capability-confirm.ts","baseline":{"blob":"0a8274d0c76c126d9b726643325b66df2c3458c3","start":1521,"end":1542},"shape":{"type":"VariableDeclaration","atoms":["const","ENOUGH_RUNS","=","5"]},"context":{"before":"6949d6c673ed35a3","after":"9898c3a5ca654ecc"}},"payload":{"text":"How many test runs since a rule was added before its not being used says anything.","wrote":["Brian Jenkins"]},"author":"local","createdAt":"2026-11-22T17:11:47.671Z","updatedAt":"2026-11-22T17:11:47.671Z"}
